Third-party algorithms adapted in mispitools
============================================

The mispitools C++ kernel (src/core/) reimplements, in portable C++17,
several mutation-model algorithms whose mathematical form is taken from
the packages listed below. No source code was copied verbatim; the
algorithms were reimplemented from the published formulas and the
referenced R sources. All listed packages are GPL-compatible with
mispitools' own license.


pedmut
------

  Source:   pedmut, https://cran.r-project.org/package=pedmut
  Author:   Magnus Dehli Vigeland (NMBU)
  License:  GPL-3
  Used in:  src/core/mutation_models.cpp

  - mutation_matrix_asymmetric() (Dawid 2002 unified asymmetric /
    reversible model): formula adapted from pedmut v0.9.0,
    R/mutationMatrix.R, function .dawid().
  - dawid_max_rate(): undefined-model rate cap adapted from pedmut
    v0.9.0, function maxRate() (the UW bound used by
    stepwiseReversible()).

  Reference: Dawid A.P. (2002), "Properties of diagnostic data
  distributions", Biometrics 58.


Familias
--------

  Source:   Familias, https://cran.r-project.org/package=Familias
  License:  GPL-3

  Used as a cross-check oracle (Suggests) only; no algorithm is
  adapted from Familias at this time. The stepwise and proportional
  models referenced in src/core/DESIGN.md will be attributed here if
  and when they are lifted.
